# WebSocket API Testing for Omni Backend
# Use this file with VS Code REST Client extension
# Install: https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=humao.rest-client

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@wsUrl = ws://localhost:8000
@chatId = test-vscode-{{$timestamp}}

### 1. Check if server is running
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 2. Get API documentation
GET {{baseUrl}}/autogen/api/v1/docs

### 3. Test WebSocket connection (This won't work in REST Client, use the HTML file instead)
# WebSocket connections cannot be tested directly with REST Client
# Use the test_websocket.html file in a browser instead
# URL: {{wsUrl}}/ws/runs/{{chatId}}

### 4. Health check endpoint (if available)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 5. Check WebSocket endpoint in browser
# Open this URL in browser for testing:
# file:///{{$workspaceRoot}}/test_websocket.html

### 6. Alternative: Test with curl (copy and paste into terminal)
# curl -i -N -H "Connection: Upgrade" \
#      -H "Upgrade: websocket" \
#      -H "Sec-WebSocket-Version: 13" \
#      -H "Sec-WebSocket-Key: SGVsbG8sIHdvcmxkIQ==" \
#      {{wsUrl}}/ws/runs/test-curl-client

### 7. Test with Node.js script
# Run in terminal: node test_websocket.js

### 8. Test with Python script  
# Run in terminal: python test_websocket.py

###############################################
# WEBSOCKET MESSAGE EXAMPLES
# Use these in the HTML test client
###############################################

### Ping Message
#{
#  "type": "ping"
#}

### Start Message
#{
#  "type": "start",
#  "task": "Hello! Can you help me with a simple task?"
#}

### Stop Message
#{
#  "type": "stop",
#  "reason": "User requested stop"
#}

### Input Response Message
#{
#  "type": "input_response", 
#  "response": "Yes, please continue"
#}

### Custom Message
#{
#  "type": "custom_action",
#  "data": {
#    "action": "test",
#    "parameters": ["param1", "param2"]
#  }
#}

###############################################
# TESTING INSTRUCTIONS
###############################################

# 1. Make sure your Omni Backend is running:
#    python main.py
#
# 2. Open test_websocket.html in a browser to test WebSocket connections
#
# 3. For automated testing, run:
#    node test_websocket.js (requires: npm install ws)
#    python test_websocket.py (requires: pip install websockets)
#
# 4. Expected WebSocket URL format:
#    ws://localhost:8000/ws/runs/{chat_id}
#
# 5. Valid message types your server accepts:
#    - ping: Simple ping message
#    - start: Start a new task/conversation
#    - stop: Stop current task
#    - input_response: Respond to server input request
#
# 6. Server responses you might receive:
#    - pong: Response to ping
#    - error: Error messages
#    - Various task-specific responses
#
# 7. Troubleshooting:
#    - Check if server is running on port 8000
#    - Verify WebSocket route is properly configured
#    - Check browser console for JavaScript errors
#    - Monitor server logs for connection attempts
